sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User (stdin)
    participant D as Debugger
    participant K as Kernel
    participant T as Tracee

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 1a: Launch (debug=true) ──
    D->>K: fork + exec with PTRACE_TRACEME
    Note over T: Child calls exec → kernel sends SIGTRAP
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS (trace stop)
    Note over D: Debugger BLOCKED
    D->>K: wait4(pid) — blocks until tracee stops
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGTRAP)
    Note over D: Debugger UNBLOCKED
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs(pid) — read GPRs
    K-->>D: returns GPR values
    D->>K: PTRACE_GETFPREGS(pid) — read FP regs
    K-->>D: returns FP register values
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKUSER × 8 — read debug regs
    K-->>D: returns debug register values
    Note over D: Registers cached in ThreadState.Regs (per-thread)
    Note over T: Tracee remains STOPPED

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 1b: Attach (PTRACE_SEIZE) ──
    D->>K: PTRACE_SEIZE(pid) — attach without SIGSTOP
    D->>K: PTRACE_INTERRUPT(pid) — request stop
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS (ptrace-stop)
    Note over D: Debugger BLOCKED
    D->>K: wait4(pid) — blocks until tracee stops
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped)
    Note over D: Debugger UNBLOCKED
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs(pid) — read GPRs
    K-->>D: returns GPR values
    D->>K: PTRACE_GETFPREGS(pid) — read FP regs
    K-->>D: returns FP register values
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKUSER × 8 — read debug regs
    K-->>D: returns debug register values
    Note over D: Registers cached in ThreadState.Regs (per-thread)
    Note over T: Tracee remains STOPPED

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 1c: ELF loading (Target) ──
    D->>K: open(program) — read ELF binary
    K-->>D: file descriptor
    Note over D: Parse ELF header, symbol table (.symtab)
    Note over D: Build symbolsByName map + sorted symbolsByAddr
    Note over D: Load DWARF sections (.debug_info, .debug_line, ...)
    Note over D: Walk DIE tree → build funcsByAddr + funcsByName indexes
    Note over D: Load CFI sections (.eh_frame, .eh_frame_hdr)
    Note over D: Parse .eh_frame_hdr → binary search table for FDE lookup
    D->>K: read /proc/<pid>/auxv — auxiliary vector
    K-->>D: array of {tag, value} pairs
    Note over D: Extract AT_ENTRY (tag 9) = actual entry point
    Note over D: loadBias = AT_ENTRY - elf.Entry
    Note over D: Propagate loadBias to both ELF and DWARF
    Note over D: For non-PIE: loadBias = 0
    Note over D: For PIE: loadBias = ASLR base offset

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 1d: Shared library discovery ──
    Note over D: Check main ELF for PT_INTERP segment
    alt Dynamic executable (has INTERP)
        Note over D: Read AT_ENTRY from auxv → real entry point
        D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA(pid, entryAddr) — install BP
        K-->>D: original byte
        D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA(pid, entryAddr, 0xCC)
        K-->>D: success
        Note over D: Install hit handler on entry-point BP
        D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0) — resume past dynamic linker
        Note over T: Dynamic linker runs: maps shared libraries
        Note over T: Tracee hits entry-point BP → STOPS
        D->>K: wait4(pid)
        K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (SIGTRAP)
        D->>K: PtraceGetRegs
        K-->>D: register values
        Note over D: Entry-point BP handler fires:
        Note over D: 1. Read .dynamic section from inferior memory
        Note over D: 2. Find DT_DEBUG entry → r_debug address
        Note over D: 3. Read r_debug.r_map → linked list of libraries
        Note over D: 4. For each link_map entry:
        Note over D:    - Read library path from inferior
        Note over D:    - OpenELF(path) → parse symbols, DWARF, CFI
        Note over D:    - Set load bias from link_map.l_addr
        Note over D:    - Add to ELFCollection
        Note over D: 5. Read r_debug.r_brk → set BP on _dl_debug_state
        Note over D: 6. Remove entry-point BP (one-shot)
        Note over T: Tracee STOPPED at program entry point
    else Static executable (no INTERP)
        Note over D: No dynamic linker — skip library discovery
    end

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 2: REPL loop ──
    D->>U: print prompt "(toydbg) "
    Note over D: Debugger BLOCKED on readline
    Note over T: Tracee still STOPPED
    U-->>D: types "continue"
    Note over D: Debugger UNBLOCKED

    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0)
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution
    Note over D: Debugger BLOCKED
    D->>K: wait4(pid) — blocks until tracee stops
    Note over T: Tracee hits breakpoint / exits / gets signal
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS again
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
    Note over D: Debugger UNBLOCKED
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values
    Note over D: Registers cached in ThreadState.Regs (per-thread)

    Note over D: Find ELF for PC: ELFContainingAddress(PC) or fallback to mainELF
    Note over D: If shared library ELF: prefix = "libname.so`"
    Note over D: Try DWARF.FunctionContainingPC(PC) + PCToSourceLocation(PC)
    Note over D: Fallback: ELF.FunctionContainingAddress(PC) (symtab only)
    D->>U: print stop reason (with PC, function name, source location)
    D->>U: print prompt "(toydbg) "
    Note over D: Debugger BLOCKED on readline again
    Note over T: Tracee STOPPED again
    Note over D,T: ── cycle repeats ──

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 3: Register commands ──
    U-->>D: types "register read rax"
    Note over D: Lookup "rax" in register table
    Note over D: Read from cached register state
    D->>U: print "rax          0x00000000cafebabe"

    U-->>D: types "register write rax 0xdeadbeef"
    Note over D: Parse "0xdeadbeef" → uint64
    Note over D: Update local register cache
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, offset, value)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "rax          0x00000000deadbeef"

    U-->>D: types "register read" (no args)
    Note over D: Iterate GPRs in register table
    D->>U: print all 25 GPR values

    U-->>D: types "register read all"
    Note over D: Iterate all 125 registers
    D->>U: print all register values

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 4: Breakpoint set / hit / resume ──
    U-->>D: types "breakpoint set 0x401000"
    Note over D: CreateBreakpointSite(0x401000)
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA(pid, 0x401000)
    K-->>D: returns original word (saved byte = low byte)
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA(pid, 0x401000, word with 0xCC)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "breakpoint 1 set at 0x401000"

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0)
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution
    Note over T: Tracee hits 0xCC at 0x401000 → SIGTRAP
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS, RIP = 0x401001 (past the 0xCC)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGTRAP)
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values (RIP = 0x401001)
    Note over D: SIGTRAP + enabled BP at PC-1 → adjust PC
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, RIP offset, 0x401000)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x401000"

    U-->>D: types "continue" (resume from breakpoint)
    Note over D: PC at enabled BP → step-over dance
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA(pid, 0x401000) — disable BP
    K-->>D: original word
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA(pid, 0x401000, restored byte)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>K: PTRACE_SINGLESTEP(pid) — execute original instruction
    Note over T: Tracee executes one instruction, STOPS
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGTRAP)
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA + POKEDATA — re-enable BP (0xCC)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0) — continue normally
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 5: Step command ──
    U-->>D: types "step"
    D->>K: PTRACE_SINGLESTEP(pid)
    Note over T: Tracee executes one instruction
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS (SIGTRAP from single step)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x401007"
    Note over D: Auto-disassemble at PC (see Phase 7)

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 6: Memory commands ──
    U-->>D: types "memory read 0x401000"
    D->>K: process_vm_readv(pid, 0x401000, 32)
    K-->>D: returns 32 bytes of tracee memory
    D->>U: print hex dump (rows of 16 bytes)

    U-->>D: types "memory read 0x401000 64"
    D->>K: process_vm_readv(pid, 0x401000, 64)
    K-->>D: returns 64 bytes
    D->>U: print hex dump

    U-->>D: types "memory write 0x7ffd1234 [0x48,0x65,0x6c]"
    Note over D: Parse byte list → [0x48, 0x65, 0x6c]
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA(pid, aligned_addr) — read-modify-write
    K-->>D: returns existing word
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA(pid, aligned_addr, modified_word)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "wrote 3 bytes at 0x7ffd1234"

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 7: Disassemble command ──
    U-->>D: types "disassemble"
    Note over D: Default: 5 instructions at current PC
    D->>K: process_vm_readv(pid, PC, 75) — read 5×15 bytes
    K-->>D: returns raw bytes
    Note over D: Patch out 0xCC from enabled breakpoints
    Note over D: Decode instructions with x86asm.Decode (64-bit mode)
    Note over D: Format each with GNUSyntax (AT&T syntax)
    D->>U: print "  0x401000: movq $0x1,%rax"
    D->>U: print "  0x401007: movq $0x1,%rdi"
    D->>U: print "  ..."

    U-->>D: types "disassemble -c 10 -a 0x401000"
    D->>K: process_vm_readv(pid, 0x401000, 150)
    K-->>D: returns raw bytes
    Note over D: Decode 10 instructions
    D->>U: print 10 disassembled instructions

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 8: Hardware breakpoint set / hit ──
    U-->>D: types "breakpoint set -h 0x401000"
    Note over D: CreateBreakpointSite(0x401000, hardware=true)
    Note over D: Find free debug register (DR0–DR3)
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, DR0 offset, 0x401000) — set address
    K-->>D: success
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, DR7 offset, control bits) — enable + mode
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "hardware breakpoint 2 set at 0x401000"
    Note over D: No memory modification (tracee bytes untouched)

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0)
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution
    Note over T: CPU hits DR0 match at 0x401000 → #DB exception
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS, RIP = 0x401000 (AT the instruction)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGTRAP)
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values (RIP = 0x401000)
    Note over D: SIGTRAP but no software BP at PC-1 → no PC adjustment
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x401000"

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 9: Watchpoint set / hit ──
    U-->>D: types "watchpoint set 0x7ffd5000 write 8"
    Note over D: CreateWatchpoint(addr, ModeWrite, size=8)
    Note over D: Check 8-byte alignment: 0x7ffd5000 & 7 == 0 ✓
    Note over D: Find free debug register (DR1)
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, DR1 offset, 0x7ffd5000)
    K-->>D: success
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEUSER(pid, DR7 offset, control bits) — write mode, 8-byte
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "watchpoint 1 set at 0x7ffd5000 (mode=write, size=8)"

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0)
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution
    Note over T: Tracee writes to 0x7ffd5000 → #DB exception
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS (SIGTRAP from debug exception)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGTRAP)
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values
    Note over D: PTRACE_GETSIGINFO → si_code=TRAP_HWBKPT
    Note over D: Read DR6 → bit 1 set → DR1 triggered
    Note over D: Lookup DR1 address → watchpoint 1
    Note over D: UpdateData() — read new value, shift old
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP at <PC> (watchpoint 1)"
    D->>U: print "Old value: 0x0  New value: 0x42"

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 10: SIGINT handling (Ctrl+C) ──
    Note over D: On launch: child gets Setpgid (own process group)
    Note over D: Debugger installs os/signal.Notify(SIGINT)
    U-->>D: presses Ctrl+C while tracee is running
    Note over D: SIGINT delivered to debugger's process group only
    Note over D: Signal handler goroutine receives SIGINT
    D->>K: kill(pid, SIGSTOP) — stop the inferior
    Note over T: Tracee receives SIGSTOP → STOPS
    D->>K: wait4(pid) — unblocks (was waiting for tracee)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by SIGSTOP)
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGSTOP at <PC>"
    D->>U: print prompt "(toydbg) "

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 11: Enhanced stop reasons ──
    Note over D: On every SIGTRAP stop:
    Note over D: 1. Check TRACESYSGOOD bit (signal 133 = syscall)
    Note over D: 2. Else call PTRACE_GETSIGINFO for si_code
    Note over D: si_code=SI_KERNEL(0x80) → TrapSoftwareBreak
    Note over D: si_code=TRAP_TRACE(2)   → TrapSingleStep
    Note over D: si_code=TRAP_HWBKPT(4)  → TrapHardwareBreak
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x401000 (breakpoint 1)"
    Note over D: Before: "process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x401000" (no detail)

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 12: Syscall catchpoints ──
    U-->>D: types "catchpoint syscall write"
    Note over D: SetSyscallCatchPolicy(CatchSome([1]))
    D->>U: print "catching syscalls: write"

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    D->>K: PTRACE_SYSCALL(pid) — resume, stop at next syscall
    Note over T: Tracee RESUMES execution
    Note over T: Tracee enters write() syscall
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS (SIGTRAP|0x80 from TRACESYSGOOD)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by signal 133)
    D->>K: PtraceGetRegs / GETFPREGS / PeekUser
    K-->>D: register values (orig_rax=1=write)
    Note over D: Signal 133 = SIGTRAP|0x80 → syscall stop
    Note over D: orig_rax=1 → "write", entry (toggle=false→true)
    Note over D: Policy "some" + write in list → report to user
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP (syscall entry)"
    D->>U: print "syscall: write(0x1, 0x..., 0x...)"

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    D->>K: PTRACE_SYSCALL(pid)
    Note over T: write() syscall executes in kernel
    Note over T: Tracee STOPS on syscall exit (SIGTRAP|0x80)
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus (stopped by signal 133)
    Note over D: Syscall exit: toggle=true→false, rax=return value
    D->>U: print "process stopped by SIGTRAP (syscall exit)"
    D->>U: print "syscall: write returned 14"

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 13: Source-level step-in ──
    U-->>D: types "step"
    Note over D: StepIn(): get current source location (file:line)
    loop Until source line changes
        D->>K: PTRACE_SINGLESTEP(pid)
        Note over T: Tracee executes one instruction, STOPS
        D->>K: wait4(pid)
        K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
        D->>K: PtraceGetRegs — read registers
        K-->>D: register values
        Note over D: GetEntryByAddress(PC) → check file:line
        Note over D: Same line? → continue loop
    end
    Note over D: Line changed → check if at function start
    Note over D: If at function start: skip prologue
    Note over D: PrologueEndForRange(lowPC, highPC) → addr
    D->>U: print source context with ">" on current line

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 14: Source-level step-over ──
    U-->>D: types "next"
    Note over D: StepOver(): get current source location
    loop Until source line changes
        Note over D: Decode instruction at PC via x86asm.Decode
        alt Current instruction is CALL
            Note over D: Compute return addr = PC + instruction length
            Note over D: Create internal breakpoint at return addr
            D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA — write 0xCC at return addr
            K-->>D: success
            D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0) — resume over the CALL
            Note over T: Tracee enters function, executes, returns
            Note over T: Tracee hits temp breakpoint → STOPS
            D->>K: wait4(pid)
            K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
            Note over D: Remove internal breakpoint
        else Not a CALL
            D->>K: PTRACE_SINGLESTEP(pid)
            Note over T: Tracee executes one instruction, STOPS
            D->>K: wait4(pid)
            K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
        end
        D->>K: PtraceGetRegs — read registers
        K-->>D: register values
        Note over D: GetEntryByAddress(PC) → check file:line
    end
    D->>U: print source context

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 15: Source-level step-out (CFI-based) ──
    U-->>D: types "finish"
    Note over D: StepOut(): check inline stack
    alt Deepest frame is inlined
        Note over D: target = end of inlined range + loadBias
    else Regular function frame (CFI unwinding)
        Note over D: FDEForPC(PC) → find matching FDE
        Note over D: Execute CIE initial instructions → baseline rules
        Note over D: Execute FDE instructions until location > PC
        Note over D: Compute CFA = register[cfa.reg] + cfa.offset
        Note over D: Apply register rules → unwound register set
        Note over D: Return address = unwound RIP
        Note over D: Fallback: read [rbp+8] if CFI unavailable
    end
    Note over D: RunUntilAddress(returnAddr)
    Note over D: Create internal breakpoint at returnAddr
    D->>K: PTRACE_POKEDATA — write 0xCC
    D->>K: PtraceCont(pid, 0)
    Note over T: Tracee executes until return addr → STOPS
    D->>K: wait4(pid)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus
    Note over D: Remove internal breakpoint
    D->>U: print source context (now in caller)

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 16: Source-level breakpoint set ──
    U-->>D: types "breakpoint set add"
    Note over D: SetBreakpointAtFunction("add")
    Note over D: Search all ELFs (main + shared libs) for function "add"
    Note over D: For each match: PrologueEndForRange → skip prologue
    Note over D: Adjust address by load bias
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA + POKEDATA — insert 0xCC
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "breakpoint 1 set at 0x... (function add)"

    U-->>D: types "breakpoint set main.c:42"
    Note over D: SetBreakpointAtLine("main.c", 42)
    Note over D: Search all ELFs for entries at main.c:42
    Note over D: If address is function start: skip prologue
    D->>K: PTRACE_PEEKDATA + POKEDATA — insert 0xCC
    K-->>D: success
    D->>U: print "breakpoint 2 set at 0x... (main.c:42)"

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 17: Source display ──
    U-->>D: types "list"
    Note over D: SourceLocationAtPC() → file, line
    Note over D: Open source file, read lines
    D->>U: print surrounding lines with ">" marker

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 18: Backtrace (stack unwinding) ──
    U-->>D: types "backtrace"
    Note over D: UnwindStack(): start at current PC + registers
    loop For each physical frame
        Note over D: ELFContainingAddress(PC) → find per-frame ELF
        Note over D: Tag frames with ELFFilename (e.g. "libcalc.so")
        Note over D: InlineStackAtAddress(PC) → check for inlined frames
        Note over D: Create StackFrame(s) for this PC
        Note over D: FDEForPC(PC) from per-frame ELF's CFI
        Note over D: Execute CIE + FDE CFI instructions
        Note over D: Compute CFA, apply register rules → caller regs
        Note over D: New PC = unwound RIP - 1 (point into call instruction)
    end
    Note over D: FormatBacktrace: qualify names with ELF filename (e.g. "libcalc.so`func")
    D->>U: print backtrace (frame index, PC, function, source location)

    Note over D,T: ── Phase 19: Multithreading (all-stop mode) ──
    Note over D: Target calls EnableThreadTracking()
    D->>K: PTRACE_SETOPTIONS(pid, TRACESYSGOOD | TRACECLONE)
    K-->>D: success
    Note over D: Clone events now notify debugger of new threads

    U-->>D: types "continue"
    Note over D: ResumeAllThreads(): two-pass approach
    Note over D: Pass 1: stepOverBreakpoint for each stopped thread
    Note over D: Pass 2: sendContinue for each stopped thread
    D->>K: PtraceCont(tid1, 0), PtraceCont(tid2, 0), ...
    Note over T: All threads RESUME execution

    Note over T: Thread N calls clone() → kernel creates new thread
    Note over T: Parent thread N STOPS (PTRACE_EVENT_CLONE)
    D->>K: wait4(-1, __WALL) — any thread
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus for tid N (clone event)
    Note over D: handleSignal: TrapClone → resume parent
    D->>K: PtraceCont(tidN, 0) — resume parent
    Note over D: New child thread sends initial SIGSTOP
    D->>K: wait4(-1, __WALL)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus for new tid (SIGSTOP)
    Note over D: handleSignal: new thread → create ThreadState
    D->>K: PTRACE_SETOPTIONS(newTid, TRACESYSGOOD | TRACECLONE)
    Note over D: Resume new thread too
    D->>K: PtraceCont(newTid, 0)

    Note over T: Thread M hits breakpoint → SIGTRAP
    Note over T: Thread M STOPS
    D->>K: wait4(-1, __WALL)
    K-->>D: returns WaitStatus for tid M
    Note over D: All-stop: stop all other running threads
    D->>K: tgkill(pid, tid1, SIGSTOP)
    D->>K: tgkill(pid, tid2, SIGSTOP)
    D->>K: wait4(tid1, __WALL), wait4(tid2, __WALL)
    K-->>D: each thread stops
    Note over D: If thread stopped by non-SIGSTOP: mark PendingSigstop
    Note over D: Set currentThread = M
    D->>U: print "thread M: process stopped by SIGTRAP at 0x..."

    U-->>D: types "thread list"
    Note over D: Iterate thread map, show TIDs and states
    D->>U: print "* thread M (stopped)"
    D->>U: print "  thread N (stopped)"

    U-->>D: types "thread select N"
    Note over D: SetCurrentThread(N)
    D->>U: print "switched to thread N"
    Note over D: register/step commands now operate on thread N
